0:{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Article\",\"headline\":\"What to Consider Before Building a SaaS Product\",\"description\":\"Building a SaaS product is one of the best ways to create recurring revenue — but only if you start with the right foundation. Here's what to think about.\",\"datePublished\":\"February 2026\",\"dateModified\":\"February 2026\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"RaveSoft Digital Solutions\",\"url\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"RaveSoft Digital Solutions\",\"url\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com\",\"logo\":{\"@type\":\"ImageObject\",\"url\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com/img/logo.png\"}},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com/blog/what-to-consider-before-building-a-saas-product\"},\"image\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com/api/og?title=What%20to%20Consider%20Before%20Building%20a%20SaaS%20Product\"}"}}],["$","script",null,{"type":"application/ld+json","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Blog\",\"item\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com/blog\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"What to Consider Before Building a SaaS Product\",\"item\":\"https://ravesoftsolutions.com/blog/what-to-consider-before-building-a-saas-product\"}]}"}}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-[#050816] pt-32 pb-16 lg:pt-40","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/blog","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-300 transition-colors mb-8","children":"← Back to Blog"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 mb-5","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-blue-500/12 border border-blue-500/25 text-blue-400 text-xs font-semibold","children":"SaaS"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1 text-gray-500 text-sm","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"iconNode":[["circle",{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10","key":"1mglay"}],["path",{"d":"M12 6v6l4 2","key":"mmk7yg"}]],"className":"lucide-clock w-3.5 h-3.5"}],"7 min read"]}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-1 text-gray-500 text-sm","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M8 2v4","key":"1cmpym"}],["path",{"d":"M16 2v4","key":"4m81vk"}],["rect",{"width":"18","height":"18","x":"3","y":"4","rx":"2","key":"1hopcy"}],["path",{"d":"M3 10h18","key":"8toen8"}]],"className":"lucide-calendar w-3.5 h-3.5"}],"February 2026"]}]]}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-white leading-[1.08] tracking-tighter mb-5","children":"What to Consider Before Building a SaaS Product"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-400 text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6","children":"Building a SaaS product is one of the best ways to create recurring revenue — but only if you start with the right foundation. Here's what to think about."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2 text-gray-500 text-sm","children":[["$","$L3",null,{"iconNode":[["path",{"d":"M19 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H9a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2","key":"975kel"}],["circle",{"cx":"12","cy":"7","r":"4","key":"17ys0d"}]],"className":"lucide-user w-4 h-4"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"RaveSoft Team"}]]}]]}]}],["$","section",null,{"className":"bg-white py-16 lg:py-20","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-8 lg:px-10 lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[1fr_280px] lg:gap-16","children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"prose prose-gray prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-bold prose-headings:text-gray-900 prose-h2:text-2xl prose-h2:mt-10 prose-h2:mb-4 prose-h3:text-lg prose-h3:mt-6 prose-h3:mb-3 prose-p:text-gray-600 prose-p:leading-relaxed prose-p:mb-5 prose-li:text-gray-600 prose-ul:space-y-1 prose-a:text-blue-600 prose-a:no-underline hover:prose-a:underline","children":"$L4"}],"$L5"]}]}],"$L6"],null,"$L7"]}],"isPartial":false,"staleTime":300,"varyParams":null,"buildId":"cBwLDW4vRc31UjdmSqCh2"}
4:[["$","p",null,{"children":"Building a SaaS product is an appealing path for entrepreneurs and businesses who want to create scalable, recurring revenue from software. But the majority of SaaS products fail — not because the technology was bad, but because the foundations were not right before a single line of code was written."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Here is what to seriously consider before you start building."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"1. Do you have a clearly defined problem to solve?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The most common cause of SaaS failure is building a product that solves a problem the market does not actually have — or does not have badly enough to pay to fix. Before building, you should be able to clearly articulate: what specific problem does this solve, for whom, and why is the current solution inadequate?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"If the answer involves \"people could use this\" rather than \"there is a real, documented pain that people are actively trying to solve,\" the product has weak foundations."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"2. Have you validated demand before writing code?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Validation does not require a fully built product. It requires evidence that real people want to pay for the solution. Landing pages, early access signups, pre-sales, and even conversations with potential users all count as validation. Building an expensive product and then trying to find customers is the wrong order of operations."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"3. What is your minimum viable product (MVP)?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"An MVP is the smallest possible version of your product that delivers the core value proposition. The goal is to get real users using a real product as quickly as possible so you can learn what actually matters. Most founders try to build too much in the first version. Ruthlessly cutting scope is one of the most important skills in early SaaS development."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"4. How will you acquire customers?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Distribution is often harder than the product. Before building, you need a credible answer to: how will the first 100 customers find this product? Content, partnerships, direct outreach, paid acquisition, and community distribution are all viable — but you need a specific strategy, not a vague plan to \"market it.\""}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"5. What are your unit economics?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"SaaS profitability depends on the relationship between customer acquisition cost (CAC) and lifetime value (LTV). You need a rough model of what you will charge, how long customers will stay, and what it will cost to acquire each one. Pricing is especially important — many founders price too low to be sustainable."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"6. Are you building for a specific market or a broad one?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Vertical SaaS (built for a specific industry) is often an easier path to early traction than horizontal SaaS (built for everyone). When you serve a specific market, your messaging is precise, your sales cycles are shorter, and word of mouth within the industry accelerates growth."}],["$","h2",null,{"children":"7. Do you have the right technical partner?"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The technology decisions made in the first version of a SaaS product have lasting consequences. Architecture choices, tech stack selection, and code quality affect how fast you can iterate, how well the product scales, and how expensive it will be to maintain and grow."}],"$L8","$L9"]
